<http://data.silknow.org/object/c98d4c70-c1b4-3c52-a607-c2a2af9b5e4d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "silk lampas, 1713-14c, Venetian or French; Bizarre pattern"@en , "The outer border of the canopy is of silver tabby composed of plain tabby with a silver strip. The inner silk consists of two panels of late bizarre pattern carried out chiefly in gold and silver thread on a red satin ground with a few details brocaded in coloured silks; each is not a full width. The pattern has curling scrolls with a few semi-naturalistic flowers.\n\nThe inner silk tissue has a satin ground, the pattern bound in 3/twill. Silver and silver gilt filé and frisé form the main parts of the pattern.\n\nThe canopy is lined with white silk."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/48ec2b9e-d1d5-3cb9-8396-f54ad5bf6b7b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/1754a599-d1d4-36b9-a9ec-aaf827f8e164> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "The outer border of the canopy is of silver tabby composed of plain tabby with a silver strip. The inner silk consists of two panels of late bizarre pattern carried out chiefly in gold and silver thread on a red satin ground with a few details brocaded in coloured silks; each is not a full width. The pattern has curling scrolls with a few semi-naturalistic flowers.\n\nThe inner silk tissue has a satin ground, the pattern bound in 3/twill. Silver and silver gilt filé and frisé form the main parts of the pattern.\n\nThe canopy is lined with white silk."@en , "silk lampas, 1713-14c, Venetian or French; Bizarre pattern"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/c98d4c70-c1b4-3c52-a607-c2a2af9b5e4d/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/c98d4c70-c1b4-3c52-a607-c2a2af9b5e4d/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/c98d4c70-c1b4-3c52-a607-c2a2af9b5e4d/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/c98d4c70-c1b4-3c52-a607-c2a2af9b5e4d/dimension/3> ;
